   "updated_at": "2026-11-19T08:46:26Z",
   "body": "Current `gh` does not support this server-capability behavior. I checked 2.105.0 and the selected source build; both stop before making a request:\n\n```console\n$ gh event listen --resource (ghes.example.com/redacted) --event com.github.pull_request.review.submitted.v1\nevent subscriptions are only available on github.com\n```\n\n**Exit status:** `1`.\n\nThe 2.105.0 release describes Event Streams as a github.com-only preview, so this is a request to change client behavior rather than a regression. The proposal is clear for product and engineering review, including keeping hints limited to github.com.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Supporting reports</summary>\n\n- [Duplicate analysis](https://github.com/cli/cli/issues/15104/artifacts/1)\n\n- [Label reasoning](https://github.com/cli/cli/issues/15104/artifacts/2)\n\n- [Reproduction log](https://github.com/cli/cli/issues/15104/artifacts/3)\n\n- [Investigation notes](https://github.com/cli/cli/issues/15104/artifacts/4)\n\n</details>\n\n[Generated by issue triage](https://github.com/cli/cli/actions/runs/44489502886).\n\n<!-- gh-aw-triage-publication:{\"input\":\"262c975adbdd6a829de8e98e1f15c1376be0d1be0d88088d464f78015af59c99\",\"complete\":true} -->\n\n<!-- gh-aw-triage-reports:{\"duplicate_analysis\":1,\"label_reasoning\":2,\"reproduction_log\":3,\"investigation_notes\":4} -->\n\n<!-- gh-aw-triage:issue-triage:15104:comment-44489502886:bfab9566b33b140ffdac016fc36256d1b137adab47e8463cc69e0e1d52c5f6ef -->",
