   "created_at": "2026-11-20T14:22:42Z",
   "updated_at": "2026-11-20T14:22:42Z",
   "body": "Thanks for raising this, @mihar-22! :pray:\n\n@BagToad and I discussed this, and the github.com restriction is deliberate. Both the API and the `gh` commands are in preview and may change at any time, so we\u2019re limiting the supported scope to avoid unexpected behavior for users. For example, API behavior could eventually differ between github.com and GHES.\n\nOnce the API is stable, we can revisit this restriction, simplify the `gh` implementation, and remove any guards that are no longer needed.\n\nI\u2019m going to close this, since revisiting these guards will be a natural part of enabling Event Streams support in `gh` for GHES and GHEC.",
   "author_association": "MEMBER",
